[32m[2025-07-27 18:09:03,858] [    INFO][0m - ['ngredients:\n- 3 tablespoons olive oil\n- 2 cloves of garlic, minced\n- 2 cups chopped fresh spinach\n- 1/2 cup crumbled feta cheese\n- 4 eggs \n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chopped cooked bacon\n- 1/2 cup heavy cream\n- 1/2 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 1 9-inch pre-made pie crust \n\nDirections:\n1. Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Add the minced garlic and cook until fragrant, about one minute.\n3. Add the spinach and cook until wilted, about 5 minutes.\n4. Remove the spinach and garlic from the pan and set aside.\n5. Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F.\n6. In a large bowl, beat together the eggs, salt, and pepper.\n7. Stir in the spinach, feta, bacon, and heavy cream, mixing well.\n8. Pour the mixture into the pre-made pie crust.\n9. Top with the shredded cheddar cheese.\n10. Bake for 25-30 minutes, or until the quiche is set in the center.\n11. Let cool for 5 minutes before serving. Enjoy!<|eot_id|>\n\n'][0m
